eeks  after attending president trump's  campaign rally in tulsa oklahoma  in june many attendees including kane  did not wear masks  and there was a surge in kovid 19 cases  in tulsa  after the event the legacy of a civil  rights legend coming up mourners  including past presidents pay tribute to  john lewis  american civil rights leader john lewis  was remembered today as a man who often  got into what he called  good trouble necessary trouble in the  fight for equality  his funeral took place in atlanta which  he represented in congress for more than  three decades  he was the first of the freedom riders  the youngest speaker on the march on  washington  leader of the march from selma to  montgomery and the man known  as the conscience of congress you  may seek the funeral drew hundreds of  mourners to ebenezer baptist church  the sanctuary of reverend dr martin  luther king jr  a twelve-year-old boy a friend of lewis  read  from one of his favorite poems invictus  i'm the master of my fate  i'm the captain of my soul three former  presidents were among the mourners  george w bush barack obama and bill  clinton  he was here on a mission that was bigger  than  personal ambition obama called lewis one  of his heroes  and in his eulogy drew parallels between  the battles lewis took part in during  the civil rights movement  and protests for racial justice  happening across america  now we see it outside our windows in big  cities  and rural towns in men  and women young and old  straight americans and lgbtq americans  blacks who long for equal treatment and  whites who can no longer accept freedom  for themselves while  witnessing the subjugation of their  fellow americans  just weeks before his death lewis  visited the black lives matter plaza in  washington  and witnessed how police brutality has  ignited  national outrage in a final essay  written before he died and published in  the new york times today  lewis writes though i am gone i urge you  to answer the highest calling of your  heart  and stand up for what you truly believe  [Music]  a call to action from a towering figure  in the civil rights movement  lewis was 80 years old  [Music]  we're back in a moment  you're watching global national  [Music]  hong kong plans to open its newest field  hospital within the next three days  there are now more than 3 100 known  cases of covid19 in hong kong  the converted exhibition center will  hold up to 2 000 beds  the chinese government is helping to  build the hospital though hong kong  officials say beijing  won't be involved with medical staff and  australia is imposing some strict  new rules after a record spike in  infections  starting on sunday face masks will be  mandatory in the state of victoria  many of the 723 new infections reported  today were in the state capital  melbourne that's despite the city being  in the middle of a six-week lockdown  the premier victoria has warned  melbourne may be locked down for even  longer if the infection rate doesn't  begin  to drop brazil's president jair  bolsonaro  who often has played down the pandemic  is recovering from covid19 and now his  wife  is infected officials confirmed today  first lady michelle bolsonaro tested  positive for covid19 and in a statement  they say she's in good health  and will follow necessary precautions  brazil's science minister has also  tested positive  he's the fifth minister in bolsonaro's  government to be infected  next new hopes for new answers nasa's  latest mission to mars  it's being called the most sophisticated  mars mission in history  perseverance just blasted off and is the  latest robotic rover  designed to search for evidence of life  on the red planet  as eric sorenson reports the multi-year  mission will not only look for signs of  microbial life  it will set the stage to bring back  samples of mars  to earth a shiny new martian rover  perseverance is the precious cargo  inside this atlas rocket  zero release it's a multi-year  multi-billion dollar journey to discover  with certainty  whether there has ever been life on mars  perseverance will land here in jezreel  crater  because three and a half billion years  ago jezreel was a lake  fed by a river surrounded by an  atmosphere that may have supported life  i would imagine you know everything from  that point forward is going to be  okay what other life is out there how do  we get to it how do we study it how do  we understand it  it'll be it'll be absolutely the biggest  discovery i think in history  today mars is a dusty forbidden  landscape perseverance will roam  and survey and deploy the first  helicopter ever flown on a different  planet  so this will actually be a very much a  wright brothers moment  except on another planet with  perseverance on route  july has become rush hour to mars last  week  china launched chianwen won to orbit and  deploy a rover on the martian surface  a few days before that the united arab  emirates sent a spacecraft called hope  to study the atmosphere of mars a first  for the arab  world in space the space exploration  towards mars uae now is as a member of  the  club the three missions to mars hope  chanwin won and now perseverance have  all left earth now  because the window of opportunity only  comes every 26 months  the goal is to have the three spacecraft  intersect with the martian orbit when  the red planet is relatively nearby  the trek will still cover more than 560  million kilometers  all three will arrive at their  destination in february of 2021  seven months from now perseverance will  be the first in a series of missions not  just to explore but to gather pieces of  mars and bring them back to earth  it will drill some 30 rock cores to be  sealed in cigar-shaped tubes  future missions will collect the samples  and return them to earth in 2031.  canadian team member chris hurd can't  wait if everything goes well we'll have  really intriguing evidence  potentially for in the form of organic 